# Usage example 2 — polarity contrast.
# Design inspired by high-overlap contrast datasets; authored here, no external
# rows copied. Domain: IT infrastructure incident.
#
# Messages: "Is the network down on server7?" and "Is it true that the network
# is not down on server7?" The two programs differ only by explicit negation,
# so they must not answer the same way: the positive claim has support, the
# negated claim is refuted by that same evidence.
@question query
  where match
    relation "network down"
    role subject "server7"
    polarity affirmed
  end

# --- contrast ---
@question query
  where match
    relation "network down"
    role subject "server7"
    polarity negated
  end
